        <IRI>#DSTChokeSize</IRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">The choke is a type of orifice installed in a well flow line for the purpose of restricting the flow and controlling the rate of production. During testing of a well, the flow will often be measured through a series of different choke diameters. (column: wlbDstChokeSize)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
