    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#definition"/>
        <IRI>#ShallowWell</IRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Shallow boreholes are defined in Section 2 of the Resource Management Regulations: Holes drilled in order to acquire information on the properties of the rock and/or to conduct geotechnical surveys to determine the location of facilities, and which are not drilled to prove or delimit a petroleum deposit or to produce or inject petroleum, water or other medium.  In reality, the definition includes two types of boreholes that are regulated by different provisions:      1. For route surveys and other soil surveys, boreholes can be drilled to study the subsurface before a facility is placed. These boreholes cannot be drilled deeper than 200 metres below the seabed, cf. Section 30 of the Petroleum Regulations.     2. When exploring for petroleum, “shallow drillings” can be carried out, cf. Section 4 of the Petroleum Regulations. These are boreholes that are drilled to acquire data on geological development of the rocks to explore for petroleum. In addition to the information on the geology at the drill site, the information can be linked with seismic data to calibrate seismic reflectors against geological units and to depth-convert seismic data. These boreholes previously had a depth restriction of 200 metres, but the Norwegian Petroleum Directorate (NPD) can now stipulate the depth. For drilling deeper than 200 metres below the seabed, an application for consent must be submitted to the Petroleum Safety Authority Norway, in addition to registration of the borehole with the NPD, cf. Section 25 of the Management Regulations.  Source: http://www.npd.no/en/Topics/Wells/Temaartikler/Established-practice-for-well-designation/</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:isDefinedBy"/>
        <IRI>#ShallowWell</IRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">http://sws.ifi.uio.no/vocab/version/20130919/npd-well</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="#definition"/>
        <IRI>#ShallowWellbore</IRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Hole drilled in order to acquire information on the rock characteristics and/or carry out geotechnical examinations for the location of installationsand which are not drilled to discover or delimit a petroleum deposit or to produce or inject petroleum, water or other medium.  Source: http://www.npd.no/en/About-us/Information-services/Dictionary/ </Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://sws.ifi.uio.no/vocab/sql#columns"/>
        <IRI>#ShallowWellbore</IRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">dateSyncNPD,wlbCompletionDate,wlbCompletionYear,wlbDateUpdated,wlbDateUpdatedMax,wlbDrillPermit,wlbDrillingFacility,wlbDrillingOperator,wlbEntryDate,wlbEntryYear,wlbEwCode,wlbEwDeg,wlbEwDesDeg,wlbEwMin,wlbEwSec,wlbEwUtm,wlbGeodeticDatum,wlbMainArea,wlbNamePart1,wlbNamePart2,wlbNamePart3,wlbNamePart4,wlbNamePart5,wlbNamePart6,wlbNpdidWellbore,wlbNsCode,wlbNsDecDeg,wlbNsDeg,wlbNsMin,wlbNsSec,wlbNsUtm,wlbProductionLicence,wlbSeismicLocation,wlbTotalDepth,wlbUtmZone,wlbWaterDepth,wlbWell,wlbWellboreName (table: wellbore_shallow_all)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://sws.ifi.uio.no/vocab/sql#label"/>
        <IRI>#ShallowWellbore</IRI>
        <Literal datatypeIRI="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#PlainLiteral">Wellbore: Shallow (table: wellbore_shallow_all)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
